---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import Code from "../../components/docs/Code.astro";
import Callout from "../../components/docs/Callout.astro";
import Endpoint from "../../components/docs/Endpoint.astro";
import Params from "../../components/docs/Params.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Authentication" lead="Your servers call the API with an API key. People can also sign in to the optional dashboard. Both reach the same tenant: your workspace and everything in it." slug="authentication">
        <h2 id="api-keys">API keys</h2>
        <p>Send your key as a bearer token on every request:</p>
        <Code tabs={[{ label: "Header", lang: "text", code: `Authorization: Bearer vk_prod_3f9a1c2b7d4e_…` }]} />
        <p>
          A key looks like <code>vk_&lt;env&gt;_&lt;prefix&gt;_&lt;secret&gt;</code>, where
          <code>env</code> is <code>dev</code> or <code>prod</code>. Each key belongs to one
          tenant, and everything you create or read with it belongs to that tenant. The full
          key is shown <strong>once</strong>, when you create it, so store it somewhere safe.
        </p>
        <Callout kind="warn">
          Keep API keys on your servers. A key gives full access to your tenant's calls,
          agents and connections. Never put one in a browser or mobile app.
        </Callout>

        <h2 id="first-key">Your first key</h2>
        <p>
          Creating a key through the API needs a key, so the first one comes from the admin
          command line: <code>python -m app.admin create-tenant</code> on a deployment, or
          <code>seed-dev</code> locally. See <a href="/docs/deploying/#bootstrap">Deploying</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 id="create">Create a key</h2>
        <Endpoint method="POST" path="/v1/api-keys" />
        <Params rows={[
          { name: "name", type: "string", desc: "A label so you can recognise the key later." },
          { name: "expires_in_days", type: "int", desc: "The key stops working after this many days (1 to 3650). Leave it out for a key that never expires." },
        ]} />
        <Code tabs={[{ label: "cURL", lang: "bash", code: `curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/v1/api-keys \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $OFFHOOK_KEY" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -d '{ "name": "production backend" }'` }, { label: "Response", lang: "json", code: `{
  "id": "5e2a9c41-7b3d-4f1e-a8c6-2d9b4e7f1a03",
  "prefix": "3f9a1c2b7d4e",
  "key": "vk_prod_3f9a1c2b7d4e_…",
  "expires_at": null,
  "created_at": "2026-10-15T10:00:00Z"
}` }]} />
        <Callout kind="note">This response is the only time the full key is returned.</Callout>

        <h2 id="list">List keys</h2>
        <Endpoint method="GET" path="/v1/api-keys" />
        <p>Returns each key's prefix, name, last use, expiry and revocation time. Never the key itself.</p>

        <h2 id="revoke">Revoke a key</h2>
        <Endpoint method="DELETE" path="/v1/api-keys/{id}" />
        <p>Revocation takes effect immediately. The next request with that key gets <code>401</code>.</p>

        <h2 id="dashboard">Dashboard sign-in</h2>
        <p>
          If you run the optional dashboard, people sign in with
          <a href="https://clerk.com">Clerk</a>. A person's first sign-in creates a tenant for
          them, and they can create API keys from there. See
          <a href="/docs/configuration/#dashboard">Configuration</a> for the Clerk settings.
        </p>

        <h2 id="errors">Errors</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><code>401</code>: the key is missing, malformed, wrong, expired or revoked.</li>
          <li><code>403</code>: the key's tenant has been deactivated.</li>
        </ul>

</DocsLayout>
